skill: "ap-ar-aging-schedules"
sections[3]:
  - "# ap-ar-aging-schedules\n\nProduce the receivables and payables aging schedules with dispute flags and cash-impact summary. Use at each period close, when treasury needs the collection outlook, or when an invoice ages past 60 days and needs a named next action. This is the feed that daily-cashflow-forecast and collections-dunning-automation run on.\n\nOwner: role-accounts-manager (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"open AR invoice export; open AP invoice export; dispute register disputes.toon; credit notes and unapplied payments\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/ar-aging.toon and ap-aging.toon with buckets 0-30|31-60|61-90|90+, dispute_flags[], dso/dpo; cash-impact summary block\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Export open AR and AP invoices at the close date; assert the export date matches the close date or the schedules are marked as of the export date and not the close.\n2. Apply credit notes and unapplied payments to the correct invoices before bucketing; an unapplied credit is an open item, not a suggestion of payment.\n3. Bucket every invoice by days outstanding: 0-30, 31-60, 61-90, 90+; boundary days are computed in minor units of days from due date, not invoice date, per the schedule policy.\n4. Flag disputed invoices from disputes.toon; a disputed invoice keeps its bucket but is excluded from the payable commitment summary until the dispute resolves.\n5. Compute DSO and DPO with run_command on the same basis as prior periods; basis changes are recorded in the artifact, never silent.\n6. Summarize cash impact: collectible AR in the next 30 days by probability band, and committed AP by due date; this block is what daily-cashflow-forecast reads.\n7. Emit ask_question for invoices in 90+ without a logged next action; the schedule is not final while any 90+ item is unactioned.\n8. Write ar-aging.toon and ap-aging.toon; hand the 61-90 AR slice to collections-dunning-automation and the cash-impact block to treasury.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\naging to daily-cashflow-forecast; 61-90 slice to collections-dunning-automation.\n"
